**Issue**: #538
**Date**: 2026-11-08
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: Rich Nunley
**Related Spec**: specs/535-make-sdlc-execute-stage-models-and-efforts-configurable-per-project-via-steering-sdlc-models-json/

# File: scripts/__tests__/features/execute-subagents.feature
# Generated from: specs/538-replace-herdr-panes-with-hooks-module-subagents-for-sdlc-execute/requirements.md
Feature: Hooks-module subagent workers for /sdlc-execute

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Stages run as hooks-module subagents without Herdr
    Given an approved spec-created issue and an Opus session with no HERDR_ environment variables
    When the person runs "/sdlc-execute #N"
    Then each dispatched stage runs as a subagent of type "nmg-sdlc:execute-<entry>" spawned by the hooks module
    And no "herdr" command is invoked
    And the issue's exact-head PR is merged and the issue is closed under the full-green gate

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Stage subagents use the configured model and effort
    Given steering/sdlc-models.json sets verify to "sonnet"/"max", repair to "opencode-go/kimi-k3.1-pro"/"default"
    When the controller dispatches verify and then redispatches it as a repair
    Then the verify subagent's model steps use "sonnet" with effort "max"
    And the repair subagent registers model "opencode-go/kimi-k3.1-pro" with no effort and its step effort is left unchanged

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Invalid configuration stops before any subagent starts
    Given steering/sdlc-models.json sets verify.effort to "extreme"
    When /sdlc-execute starts
    Then it exits 2 with "steering/sdlc-models.json: verify.effort" in the diagnostic
    And no git or gh command runs and no spawn request is written

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Check-in reports carry the worker's activity
    Given an implement subagent whose last tool call was 300 seconds ago
    When the check-in interval of 300 seconds elapses
    Then the check-in report has reason "activity_unchanged" and an activity object with recent tool calls, latest transcript text and seconds since last activity
    And the idle supervising session receives a prompt to fetch and answer the report

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Prompt guidance enters the running worker's conversation
    Given a running verify subagent
    When the supervising session decides prompt with text "Re-run the failing contract test"
    Then that text is appended to the subagent's conversation
    And the controller waits for the subagent's fresh handoff

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Redispatch stops the running worker first
    Given a running implement subagent
    When the supervising session decides redispatch
    Then the subagent is stopped with status "killed" before the replacement spawn request is written
    And any further tool call from the stopped subagent is denied

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Headless execute runs to completion and reports its status
    Given "claude -p --session-id <uuid> --plugin-dir <checkout> '/sdlc-execute #N'" on an Opus model
    When the run executes
    Then the process stays alive until the controller finishes and its last output is "#N: MERGED and CLOSED"
    And "claude -p --resume <uuid> '/sdlc-execute --result'" prints that line and exits 0

  @SCN008
  Scenario: The retain-worker flag is rejected
    Given the arguments "--retain-worker #N"
    When /sdlc-execute parses them
    Then it stops with a usage error naming "--retain-worker" before setting a goal
    And "--check-in-seconds 60 #N" still parses

  @SCN009
  Scenario: Autopilot is gone and interactive commands stay TUI-only
    Given NMG_SDLC_AUTOPILOT=1 in the environment
    When "claude -p --plugin-dir <checkout> '/sdlc-write-spec #N'" runs
    Then it prints "Run /sdlc-write-spec in the TUI." and exits 2 with no mutation
    And in a TUI session with NMG_SDLC_AUTOPILOT=1 the hooks module approves no plan and answers no question on its own

  @SCN010
  Scenario: The smoke gate delivers the verify-provisioned issue without Herdr
    Given the nmg-sdlc-smoke provider with no explicit issue queue
    And ".nmg-sdlc/smoke/provisioned.json" names an open smoke issue with "spec-created" and a merged "docs: approve spec for #N" PR
    When the gate runs
    Then it delivers that issue through a headless "claude -p --session-id <uuid> --plugin-dir <candidate> '/sdlc-execute #N'" session
    And it runs no draft-issue or write-spec command, invokes no "herdr" command, and the pass still requires the exact-head merged PR and the closed issue

  @SCN013
  Scenario: The smoke gate fails when no smoke issue was provisioned
    Given the nmg-sdlc-smoke provider with no explicit issue queue
    And no ".nmg-sdlc/smoke/provisioned.json" record, or one naming a closed issue
    When the gate runs
    Then it fails with "nmg-sdlc-smoke smoke issue not provisioned" and the reason

  @SCN014
  Scenario: The verify worker provisions the smoke issue through the real interactive commands
    Given nmg-sdlc's own verification with "repository.nmg-sdlc-smoke" registered and no recorded open smoke issue
    When the verify worker runs with the "project.smoke" snippet
    Then it drives "/sdlc-draft-issue <need>" and "/sdlc-write-spec #N" in an interactive claude session inside tmux, answering each dialog itself
    And it writes ".nmg-sdlc/smoke/provisioned.json" naming issue N once N has "spec-created" and a merged spec PR, before running the registered gates

  @SCN011
  Scenario: Upgrade rewrites the Herdr CONTRIBUTING sentence idempotently
    Given a CONTRIBUTING.md containing "drives Herdr Claude worker panes through implementation, verification, and delivery"
    When the upgrade plan applies
    Then the sentence reads "runs Claude Code stage subagents through implementation, verification, and delivery" and all other bytes are unchanged
    And a second upgrade detects nothing

  @SCN012
  Scenario: A refused worker start fails the run
    Given the hooks module denies the implement subagent spawn
    When the controller dispatches implement
    Then the run exits non-zero with "worker_start_refused" and the denial reason
    And no deliver stage runs
